{"skill":{"slug":"web-scraper","displayName":"Web Scraper"},"version":{"version":"0.1.1","createdAt":1774228654284,"changelog":"web-scraper 0.1.1\n\n- Added a CHANGELOG.md file for better tracking of updates.\n- Clarified credential handling: the skill itself never makes direct API calls, and only generated scripts reference `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` if LLM extraction is used.\n- Updated environment survey instructions to check for presence of `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` (for generated code), not the value.\n- Improved documentation for credential scope and clarified planning protocol steps.","changelogSource":"auto","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","size":568,"sha256":"094b004af018eb4349590bf80f373abec5c085f0513c1794ce55dccb675ed2dc","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":30696,"sha256":"8d43b93f5f77bd0ef40a31f3d33d503ba3bee10710a580ac4651eb75d25abcff","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"claw.json","size":857,"sha256":"878ed183288c38e61ab51de8ef4348b9be4f3314e54087aac15e1c1396f68847","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2323,"sha256":"396b71239e86bc2be30e925ab6f29f971ac6c26b2790ef6c5bc85764af7fb61b","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789081136529,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"84e6c7b47f353606aa81527172bf57d206a4ec8e4d1ae136e532e37cfed618b7","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/84e6c7b47f353606aa81527172bf57d206a4ec8e4d1ae136e532e37cfed618b7","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: web-scraper\nVersion: 0.1.1\n\nThe 'web-scraper' skill is a well-structured and documented tool for multi-stage web content extraction and analysis. It follows industry best practices such as rate limiting, robots.txt compliance, and a cascade approach to resource usage, while explicitly instructing the agent to avoid sensitive files like .env and to handle API keys securely via environment variables (SKILL.md, claw.json).","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779166537651},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":55,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":6,"checkedAt":1789081136529},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is mostly a disclosed web-scraping helper, but it includes instructions to reveal soft-paywalled content and can send scraped text to OpenRouter without a clear per-use consent gate.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Filesystem and network permissions are proportionate for creating scraper scripts, fetching pages, and writing outputs; the OpenRouter stage is disclosed and optional, but scraped content may leave the local environment when enabled.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The package is a Markdown skill with no bundled executable scripts, but it recommends unpinned pip packages and Playwright browser installation, which is normal for this tooling but not reproducible.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill has useful planning, rate-limit, robots.txt, and credential-scope rules, but its paywall instructions are internally under-scoped: it forbids hard-paywall bypass while permitting DOM manipulation for soft paywalls.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No evidence of background services, scheduled tasks, tool hijacking, credential-file reads, persistent memory writes, or privilege escalation was found; checkpoint/output persistence is ordinary scraper output.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The scraping, parsing, Playwright rendering, metadata extraction, local output files, and optional LLM entity extraction generally match the stated web-scraper purpose, but the soft-paywall guidance explicitly tells the agent to remove overlays and reveal hidden paragraphs, which goes beyond ordinary content extraction.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable supervising its use: avoid using it to reveal or collect paywalled content, do not enable the OpenRouter entity-extraction stage for private/authenticated/sensitive pages without explicit approval, and prefer pinned dependencies in an isolated environment.","findings":"[RP1] expected: The Playwright availability check uses unpinned npx resolution; this is a supply-chain reproducibility concern, but it is not hidden behavior or evidence of malicious code.\n[SQP-3] expected: The hard-coded Portuguese Accept-Language header fits the apparent PT-BR scraping focus, but users should know it can bias returned content and disclose a locale preference.\n[SSD-4] unexpected: The artifact-backed instruction to remove a soft-paywall overlay and reveal paragraphs is a material concern because it operationalizes access-restriction circumvention.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: The DOM-unhiding guidance is not necessary for normal scraping and materially increases misuse potential.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The safety section still permits soft-paywall DOM manipulation, so the concern is accepted rather than treated as a scanner-only issue.\n[SQP-2] expected: Sending up to 4000 characters of clean article text and metadata to OpenRouter supports the optional entity-extraction feature and is disclosed, but the skill lacks a clear per-use consent and sensitivity check.\n[T05] unexpected: The static scan's paywall concern is supported by the artifact's explicit soft-paywall overlay-removal instruction.\n[T09] expected: The OpenRouter data flow is purpose-aligned and documented, but should be treated carefully for private, authenticated, copyrighted, or sensitive pages.\n[T08] expected: The dependency-install guidance uses common packages for scraping, with no typosquatting or malicious source evidence; the issue is unpinned supply-chain exposure.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789081136529}}}}}